WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.960
Speaker 1: So let's talk about Vladimir Putin.&nbsp;
As many of you remember, we started talking about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:12.320
the Putin's health story a while ago at the very&nbsp;
start of the invasion of Ukraine by Russia. We got&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:18.480
emails from a couple of doctors who said, Putin&nbsp;
doesn't look good. Putin looks sick. We could be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:23.280
looking at any number of different conditions. And&nbsp;
I said to all of you, this is speculation. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:30.880
is mere idle speculation. We then saw about&nbsp;
ten days ago this video of Vladimir Putin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:36.960
where he is sitting at a table. He's gripping the&nbsp;
table almost for support. He's, like pushed back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:44.160
against the chair. He's tapping his toe. His left&nbsp;
hand is shaky. And this renewed speculation that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:50.800
there could be something very seriously wrong with&nbsp;
Vladimir Putin in the last 48 hours, a story came&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:57.840
out in the British tabloid The Sun that Putin is&nbsp;
going to be having cancer surgery. And I didn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:03.680
come to you with the story because the sun is&nbsp;
simply not an appropriate source for our show.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:11.360
That story now has made it into The New York Post.&nbsp;
Now, I still come to you with caution and I say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:16.800
The New York Post is basically the print version&nbsp;
of Fox News. It's still not a slam dunk that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:22.800
truth is exactly as is being reported here.&nbsp;
But this is now becoming mainstream enough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:26.720
that since we've been talking about&nbsp;
it at this point for over a month,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:32.160
I want to talk about it with you. The New York&nbsp;
Post story says Putin to undergo cancer surgery&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:39.680
and transfer power to the ex FSB chief. Russian&nbsp;
President Vladimir Putin is set to undergo cancer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:45.600
surgery and temporarily hand over power to a&nbsp;
hard line former federal police chief, according&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:50.960
to a new report. Putin will transfer control&nbsp;
of Russia's government to Nikolai Patrushev,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:56.720
head of the Russian Federal Police's Security&nbsp;
Council, while he is incapacitated during and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.720 --> 00:02:03.520
after the procedure, according to a video from&nbsp;
the mysterious Telegram Channel. General SVR,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:08.720
the channel is purportedly run by a former&nbsp;
Russian foreign intel service. Lieutenant general&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:16.720
reported that Putin has been told by doctors he&nbsp;
must undergo an operation. The anticipated surgery&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:24.080
and recovery are expected to incapacitate Putin&nbsp;
for a short time, according to the unconfirmed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:30.480
report. Putin is unlikely to agree to hand&nbsp;
over power for a longer period of time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:36.160
I will say that this is the worst&nbsp;
option. Patrushev is an outright villain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:41.920
no better than Putin. Moreover, he's more cunning&nbsp;
and I would say more insidious than Putin.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:50.160
If he comes to power, Russian's problems will&nbsp;
only multiply. So is this true? We don't really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:56.960
know. We don't really know. But what we do know&nbsp;
is at this point, speculation from doctors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:07.920
video evidence and this kind of strange report&nbsp;
all are saying the exact same thing. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:15.040
whether this is responsible for Putin's actions&nbsp;
in Ukraine is a different story altogether. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:18.960
the reason that the speculation is related&nbsp;
to the invasion of Ukraine would be, well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:25.440
if he believes that he's going to die, he&nbsp;
may try to go out in a sort of final blaze of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:30.480
trying to restore glory to the former&nbsp;
Soviet Union, as he still idolizes it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:36.880
or it may be a side effect of medication that is&nbsp;
making him irrational. There are also unconfirmed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:42.720
reports that this is actually a cognitive&nbsp;
issue and dementia. It's it's wild speculation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:49.760
at the micro level. But the macro story continues&nbsp;
to be more and more different types of stories&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:56.320
about Putin's health. So all we can do is wait and&nbsp;
see. And I don't even know that there's more to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.320 --> 00:04:00.800
say about it. But the story creeping, creeping,&nbsp;
creeping more and more into the mainstream.

